<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdullah Mukarram Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned <a href="/years/1778">1778</a>–<a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdullah Mukarram Shah was sultan of Kedah on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a> from 1778 to 1797. Seeking protection against Siam and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, he allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-light">Francis Light</a> of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> to occupy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penang">Penang</a> in 1786. When the British refused military help, he tried to retake the island in 1791 but was defeated and accepted an annual payment instead.</p></div>
